Then the lights went out, all of them, even the ones that are not technically lights, such as hope.

{name} crept through the dark, guided by a small circle of courage and a much larger circle of panic.

Something enormous breathed in the darkness. It smelled faintly of apples, which is my least favorite combination of facts.
